# The same brief as 07-crushline, answered without touching the grid.
#
# Four turbines drive two line shafts directly. No generator, no motor, no
# electricity anywhere in the machine: rotary is a domain, and a turbine already
# makes it, so putting it through a generator and back through a motor would be
# two conversions and 19% for nothing.
#
# What it costs is everything the power brief was trying to minimise -- a
# reactor, four exchangers, three pumps, 350 water a tick and the wasted heat of
# two heat pipes. Twenty-five components against fifteen, on twice the plot, for
# roughly the same ore. That is the trade, stated in numbers, and neither
# answer is wrong.
#
# This is also the design the note that started experiment 07 asked for: several
# machines hanging off one shared shaft, which nothing anywhere had to be told
# was allowed.

machine "Steam Crusher"
brief crush

inlet     I1  at 0,0   draws ore
crusher   C1  at 4,0
crusher   C2  at 9,0
mill      MI1 at 14,0
separator S1  at 19,0
outlet    O1  at 24,0
skip      SK1 at 24,3

shaft     SH1 at 6,5
shaft     SH2 at 16,5
gearbox   GB1 at 5,7   ratio 4

turbine   T1  at 0,5
turbine   T2  at 11,5
turbine   T3  at 22,5
turbine   T4  at 22,8

exchanger HX1 at 0,8
exchanger HX2 at 11,8
exchanger HX3 at 26,5
exchanger HX4 at 26,9

heatpipe  HP1 at 14,13
heatpipe  HP2 at 20,13
heatpipe  HP3 at 22,11

reactor   R1  at 5,12
pump      W1  at 0,12
pump      W2  at 11,12
pump      W3  at 30,7

wire I1.out -> C1.in
wire C1.out -> C2.in
wire C2.out -> MI1.in
wire MI1.out -> S1.in
wire S1.rich -> O1.solid
wire S1.tails -> SK1.solid

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire R1.heat -> HP1.in
wire HP1.out -> HP2.in
wire HP2.out -> HP3.in
wire HP3.out -> HX3.heat
wire HP3.out -> HX4.heat

wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W2.water -> HX2.water
wire W3.water -> HX3.water
wire W3.water -> HX4.water

wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T2.steam
wire HX3.steam -> T3.steam
wire HX4.steam -> T4.steam

wire T1.rotary -> SH1.in
wire T2.rotary -> SH1.in
wire T3.rotary -> SH2.in
wire T4.rotary -> SH2.in

wire SH1.out -> GB1.in
wire GB1.out -> C1.drive
wire GB1.out -> C2.drive
wire SH2.out -> MI1.drive
wire SH2.out -> S1.drive
